      "content": "Welcome to NebulaFlow, the high-performance CLI tool at GridScale engineered to automate complex infrastructure provisioning and deployment workflows for modern SRE teams. Before executing any commands, ensure your terminal environment supports bash or zsh syntax and that your local machine has write permissions to the current directory where configuration files reside. A \"cluster\" in this context refers to a logical grouping of compute nodes within a specific cloud region, such as us-east-1, which acts as the foundational resource pool for your applications. To authenticate your session securely, run `nf auth login --token <TOKEN>` by substituting the angle brackets with your unique GridScale API key stored in environment variables. Once authenticated, initialize your infrastructure by executing `nf cluster init --region us-east-1 --size small` to provision the designated node pool with the specified resource allocation parameters. Finally, deploy your application stack by running `nf deploy --config ./production.yaml`, which parses the YAML manifest to push the latest container images and service definitions to the newly created cluster. This detailed walkthrough ensures you understand the underlying mechanics of authentication, resource provisioning, and configuration parsing required for a successful deployment.",
